BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:165919@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20261102T150426Z
DTSTART:20261102T134800Z
SUMMARY:Critical Path Schedule Monitoring Election Window for the 2026 Interim Reconfiguration Auction Qualification Process is Open Until November 2\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:The window to elect critical path schedule (CPS) monitoring for all New Import Capacity Resources\, New Demand Capacity Resources with non-commercial capacity\, and New Generating Capacity Resources with non-commercial capacity is now open and will close on November 2\, 2026 at 23:59. Pursuant to Section III.13.A.2(c)(2) of the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff\, electing CPS monitoring within the CPS monitoring election window is required for all New Import Capacity Resources\, New Demand Capacity Resources with non-commercial capacity\, and New Generating Capacity Resources with non-commercial capacity to successfully complete the 2026 interim reconfiguration auction (RA) qualification process.\n\n\n\nAdditional details on how to elect CPS monitoring as part of the 2026 interim RA qualification process can be found on the ISO’s Interim RA Qualification Process website: https://www.iso-ne.com/markets-operations/markets/forward-capacity-market/fcm-participation-guide/interim-reconfiguration-auction-qualification. Participants may also view the updated “How to Elect CPS Monitoring in FCTS” video by Participant Training Services: https://vimeo.com/1012587388/c0d47dc290.\n\n\n\nContact Participant Support at (413) 540-4220 or askiso@iso-ne.com<mailto:askiso@iso-ne.com> or via an Ask ISO Case for any questions.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165919
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165919
END:VEVENT
